---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

/* Mirror the open-spots constant on the home Available section. Update both
   when capacity changes (or refactor into a shared module if you start
   adding more shared content later). */
const OPEN_SPOTS = 1;
---

<Layout
  title="Working with Ajay Raj — Independent Software Engineer · Embedded, Hardware, ML/AI"
  description="Ajay Raj — independent software engineer in San Diego (remote). Available for safety-critical or mission-critical builds, MVPs in messy scientific domains, and inherited projects to decipher and ship. Embedded systems, hardware/software co-design, production ML, AI tooling, internal tooling."
>
  <main class="card-page">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← ajayraj.co</a>

    <article class="business-card">
    <header class="card-header">
      <h1 class="card-name">Ajay Raj</h1>
      <p class="card-role">engineer for hard problems</p>
      <p class="card-specialties">embedded · hardware · ML · operating systems</p>

      <div class="card-status-row">
        <div class="card-chip card-chip-status">
          <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          Now — independent
        </div>
        {OPEN_SPOTS > 0 && (
          <div class="card-chip card-chip-warm">
            <span class="capacity-spark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            Room for <strong>{OPEN_SPOTS}</strong> more client
          </div>
        )}
        <div class="card-chip card-chip-quiet">
          <span class="location-pin" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>
          san diego · remote
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="card-aside card-aside-top">
      <p>
        <strong>Hiring for your team?</strong>
        I'd like to chat, and am open to the right role if there's alignment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card-section">
      <h2>Working with me</h2>
      <p>My clients usually have:</p>
      <ul class="card-needs">
        <li><span class="hl">safety-critical or mission-critical</span> needs that have to be met above all</li>
        <li><span class="hl">MVPs in messy scientific domains</span></li>
        <li><span class="hl">inherited projects</span> to decipher and ship</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If that sounds like you, we'll work well together.</p>
      <p>
        I enjoy messy intersections, where the science, the hardware, or the
        real world meets the code. I own products end-to-end: prototype
        quickly to iterate towards requirements and core features, then
        release. The version I ship is <span class="hl">test-driven</span>,
        <span class="hl">traceable</span>, documented, and mature enough for
        anyone to pick the work back up.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card-section">
      <h2>What I take on</h2>
      <ul class="card-fits">
        <li><strong>Embedded, firmware &amp; OS</strong> — RTOS, kernel and driver work, BSPs, FPGA, system-level performance; compliance-ready (FDA / IEC 62304 / ISO 13485 background)</li>
        <li><strong>Custom devices &amp; co-design</strong> — full builds from spec to ship: enclosure, electronics, schematic-aware firmware, mechatronic integration; blissful end products</li>
        <li><strong>Production ML</strong> — research code into systems that scale with load</li>
        <li><strong>AI systems</strong> — MCP, RAG, agents, evaluators; implemented safely, fixing vibe-slop</li>
        <li><strong>Prototype to production</strong> — quick first cuts, built to last</li>
        <li><strong>Internal tooling</strong> — tools, workflow, and documentation your team will love</li>
        <li><strong>Open-ended problems</strong> — exploratory R&amp;D, scoping unknown territory, “we don't know what this needs to be yet”</li>
        <li><strong>Architecture review &amp; rescue</strong> — audits, refactors, inherited projects, getting unstuck</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="card-section">
      <h2>How engagements typically work</h2>
      <ul class="card-engagements">
        <li><strong>Discovery</strong> — short paid scoping call or week. We figure out shape and fit before either of us commits.</li>
        <li><strong>Build</strong> — fixed-scope when the work is well-defined, hourly when the shape is still emerging.</li>
        <li><strong>Retainer</strong> — open to flexible arrangements: a committed bucket of hours plus stand-by support, for ongoing work or unpredictable needs.</li>
        <li><strong>Handoff</strong> — code, tests, docs, runbooks. I leave the work better than I found it, so the next team can pick it up cold.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="card-section card-cta">
      <h2>Let's talk</h2>
      <p>Tell me about the problem in a few sentences — happy to read a brief, repo, or rough sketch.</p>
      <div class="card-actions">
        <a href="mailto:ajay@ajayraj.co?subject=Project%20inquiry" class="cta-primary">
          ajay@ajayraj.co →
        </a>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/ajayjonathanraj" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="cta-secondary">
          LinkedIn
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    </article>

    <footer class="card-footer">
      <p>
        For background, projects, and how I think →
        <a href="/">ajayraj.co</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .card-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 6rem;
    color: #f0e8ff;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 10;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    transition: color 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .back-link:hover {
    color: #ff9966;
    border-bottom-color: #ff9966;
  }

  /* Single card wraps the whole pitch — gives the white text a defined dark
     surface to sit on (much more readable than text floating on the page
     gradient) and matches the card-everywhere aesthetic of the main site. */
  .business-card {
    background: rgba(36, 24, 53, 0.78);
    border: 1px solid rgba(190, 156, 212, 0.25);
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    padding: 2.5rem 2.5rem 2rem;
    backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
    box-shadow: 0 14px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .business-card {
      padding: 1.75rem 1.25rem 1.5rem;
      border-radius: 0.875rem;
    }
  }

  .card-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  .card-name {
    font-family: var(--font-serif, 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #f0c9d9;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    text-shadow: 1px 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  }
  .card-role {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  /* Smaller, quieter byline directly under the role — lists the specialty
     surfaces without making them the headline. */
  .card-specialties {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .card-status-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .card-chip {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .card-chip-status {
    background: rgba(122, 191, 158, 0.12);
    border: 1px solid rgba(122, 191, 158, 0.3);
    color: #7abf9e;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }
  .card-chip-warm {
    background: rgba(255, 153, 102, 0.14);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 153, 102, 0.45);
    color: #ffb88c;
  }
  .card-chip-warm strong {
    color: #ff9966;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .card-chip-quiet {
    background: transparent;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.65);
  }

  .status-dot, .capacity-spark {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .status-dot {
    background: #7abf9e;
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(122, 191, 158, 0.7);
    animation: cardStatusPulse 2.4s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  .capacity-spark {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: #ff9966;
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255, 153, 102, 0.7);
    animation: cardCapacityBlink 2.6s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  .location-pin {
    color: #ff9966;
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  @keyframes cardStatusPulse {
    0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
    50%      { opacity: 0.4; }
  }
  @keyframes cardCapacityBlink {
    0%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); }
    50%      { opacity: 0.5; transform: scale(0.85); }
  }

  .card-section {
    margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
  }
  .card-section h2 {
    /* Sans on section headings — keeps the page feeling modern.
       The serif on the H1 name carries the personality alone. */
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #f0c9d9;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }
  .card-section p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .card-fits, .card-engagements, .card-needs {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .card-fits li, .card-engagements li, .card-needs li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
  }
  .card-fits li::before, .card-engagements li::before, .card-needs li::before {
    content: "▸";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: #ff9966;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  .card-fits strong, .card-engagements strong {
    color: #ffb88c;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .card-needs {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0.85rem;
  }

  .card-cta {
    background: rgba(74, 44, 109, 0.45);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 160, 122, 0.4);
    border-radius: 0.875rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* Quiet "by the way" — italic, slightly muted, sits between engagements
     and the primary CTA without competing with either. */
  .card-aside {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid rgba(255, 160, 122, 0.45);
    background: rgba(255, 153, 102, 0.05);
    border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
  }
  /* Tighter top margin so it tucks right under the header chips */
  .card-aside-top {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
  .card-aside p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .card-aside strong {
    color: #ffb88c;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .card-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .cta-primary {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    background: #ff9966;
    color: #1f1426;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 0.625rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease, background 0.2s;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(255, 153, 102, 0.3);
  }
  .cta-primary:hover {
    background: #ffaa7a;
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 22px rgba(255, 153, 102, 0.45);
  }
  .cta-secondary {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 0.625rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(190, 156, 212, 0.4);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: background 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .cta-secondary:hover {
    background: rgba(190, 156, 212, 0.15);
    border-color: rgba(255, 160, 122, 0.5);
  }

  .card-footer {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .card-footer p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }
  .card-footer a {
    color: #ff9966;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted rgba(255, 153, 102, 0.5);
    transition: color 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .card-footer a:hover {
    color: #ffaa7a;
    border-bottom-color: #ffaa7a;
  }

  .hl {
    color: #ff9966;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255, 160, 122, 0.3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .card-page { padding: 2.5rem 1rem 4rem; }
    .card-name { font-size: 2rem; }
    .card-section h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  }
</style>
